# 🏦 Loan Rejection Funnel Analysis
### End-to-End Banking Analytics using PostgreSQL, Python & Power BI

## 📌 Project Overview

Loan approval is a critical process in the banking industry that directly impacts profitability and risk management. Financial institutions receive thousands of loan applications every month, but not every application progresses through the approval pipeline.

This project analyzes the loan application journey to identify where applicants drop off, uncover the key factors influencing approval and rejection decisions, and provide actionable insights that help improve operational efficiency while minimizing lending risk.

Using SQL, Python, and Power BI, this project performs end-to-end data analysis—from data preparation and exploratory analysis to interactive dashboard development and business recommendations.



## 🎯 Business Problem

Banks aim to maximize loan approvals without increasing the risk of loan defaults. However, many applications are rejected due to factors such as insufficient income, poor credit history, incomplete documentation, or high financial risk.

The challenge is to identify:

- Where applicants exit the loan approval process.
- Which customer segments experience the highest rejection rates.
- Which financial and demographic factors contribute most to loan rejection.
- How the approval process can be optimized while maintaining healthy lending standards.


## 🚀 Objectives

- Analyze the complete loan application funnel.
- Measure conversion rates at each stage of the approval process.
- Identify the major reasons behind loan rejections.
- Evaluate customer demographics and financial characteristics.
- Discover patterns associated with high-risk applicants.
- Build an interactive Power BI dashboard for business stakeholders.
- Provide data-driven recommendations to improve approval efficiency and reduce risk.



